course: dictionary
lesson: 13122
title: Up and down: fluctuate
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Fluctuate is a formal word. It means to keep changing, going up and down, especially in amount, level or price. You will meet it in maths, science and exam questions.
explain: «The temperature fluctuated throughout the day.» The clue is «throughout the day». The temperature did not rise once and stop. It kept moving up and down. Try swapping in changed: the sentence still makes sense, but fluctuated is more exact because it shows the movement going up and down again and again.
explain: Many things can fluctuate. «Ben's mood fluctuated during the football match»: he was happy when his team scored, cross when they missed, and happy again at the end. Prices and weather can fluctuate too, and graphs in science often show numbers that fluctuate.
fact: Fluctuate is a verb. Its forms are fluctuate, fluctuates, fluctuated and fluctuating.
fact: «Fluctuate» means to keep changing, going up and down.
fact: It is often used for amount, level or price: «Petrol prices fluctuate from week to week.»
fact: Fluctuate is formal, so you will see it more in writing and exams than in everyday chat.
fact: A graph that fluctuates goes up and down rather than moving in one straight line.
exercise: «The temperature fluctuated throughout the day.» What does fluctuated mean? | Froze solid and stopped | *Went up and down | Stayed exactly the same all day | Fell once and never rose again
exercise: Fill the gap: «Yesterday the price ___ wildly.» | fell and stayed | stopped | *fluctuated | froze
exercise: Why might an author choose fluctuate instead of change? | It is only used for animals | It is shorter and easier to spell | It means the same as stop | *It is more formal and shows repeated up and down movement
test: «The weather fluctuated all week, from sunny to stormy and back again.» What does fluctuated mean? | Stayed still | Got colder every day | Was cancelled | *Kept changing up and down
test: Fill the gap: «The ball's speed ___ as it bounced across the field.» | *fluctuated | ended | stood | slept
exam: Which best describes something that fluctuates? | It disappears completely | It is always free | *It goes up and down over time | It stays the same for ever
